  "structure": "Ten required 6 EC units in each of years one and two for this pathway. In year three, 30 EC of elective study, two advanced subjects from the three specialist options, Financial Econometrics from the broader choices and a 12 EC thesis. This choice satisfies the chart and guide. Noncredit study support and English diagnostic/refresher obligations do not add credits. The 42 EC BSA combines passes from calculus/analysis and probability/statistics. Minor entry normally needs 90 EC and the relevant approval and level requirements. Honours remains outside the degree.",
  "progression": "The adopted 2026–2027 chart and annual guide establish 60 EC in each year. The first year has ten required 6 EC units, plus noncredit study support and language obligations. The second year has ten 6 EC units including three part-II courses. One part-II replacement needs permission. The selected third year has 30 EC of elective study, Econometrics III, Mathematical Economics III, Financial Econometrics and a 12 EC thesis. The choice uses one broader elective and satisfies both the guide’s one-or-two rule and the chart’s at-most-two rule. The Econometrics III module code resolves the inconsistent title in the chart. The Integrative Practical requires a first-period partial grade of 5.5 or higher from one of the three part-I subjects. The Advanced Practical requires one pass from each of the probability/statistics, programming/numerical methods and part-I subject groups. The Econometrics thesis requires 120 EC including Econometrics II. Financial Econometrics follows Econometrics III. Keep the minor approval, level and non-overlap rules separate from the required credits.",
  "interestAccounting": "All 36 exact rows assessed. Twelve direct or stable rows are addressed through the core, a viable distinct energy direction or tested alternatives. Eleven curricular topics support the review. Three illustrations and ten outcomes do not independently generate a direction.",
